event: content_block_start
data: {"type":"content_block_start","index":5,"content_block":{"type":"code_execution_tool_result","tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015yo7dv3uo5Nq58wDfLkR43","content":{"type":"code_execution_result","stdout":"<class 'str'> 15536\n[{\"type\": \"web_search_result\", \"title\": \"Austin Texas\", \"url\": \"https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/7304328db79344c2897176f32951bfde\", \"content\": \"The city of Austin Texas was founded In December of 1839.\\n\\n# Austin Texas\\nAustin is the southernmost state capital of the contiguous 48 states, is located in Central\\u00a0Texas.\\u00a0Austin\\u00a0is 146 miles northwest of Houston which is the largest and the capital city in Texas.\\n\\n**History of Austin**\\n\\nThe city of Austin Texas was founded In December of 1839. It is the capital of Texas and was named in the honor of Stephan F. Austin. It was formerly known as Waterloo city.\\n\\nIn 1888 civic leader Alexander P. Wooldridge proposed the building of a dam across the Colorado River and use water power to attract manufacturing. Although the Dam was not complete, the town is now emerging and attracting others around the area, but in contrast it still could not sustain the size of the population.\\n\\nAustin had only one paved street thought-out the whole city due to\\u00a0the heavy municipal indebtedness incurred in building the dam which resulted in the neglect of city services. In 1905 Austin had few sanitary sewers, virtually no public parks or playgrounds.\\n\\nThe city of Austin Texas was founded In December of 1839. It is the capital of Texas and was named in the honor of Stephan F. Austin. It was formerly known as Waterloo city.\\n\\nAustin was flourishing after being established as a city and was doing great until about 1942 when the Mexican troops captured San Antonio to take back Texas. It was then an executive order from Sam Houston to move the national Archives from Austin to Houston for safekeeping. This did not go through and the national archives remained in Austin.\", \"page_age\": \"2186 days ago\"}, {\"type\": \"web_search_result\", \"title\": \"History of the city of Austin, Texas\", \"url\": \"https://www.britannica.com/summary/Austin-Texas\", \"content\": \"Austin, Texas(more). Austin, City (pop., 2020: 961,855), capital of Texas, U.S. It was founded in 1835 as the village of Waterloo on the Colorado River in south-central Texas. In 1839 it was made capital of the Republic of Texas and renamed ...\\n\\n# Austin summary\\n## Discover interesting historical facts about Austin, Texas\\n**Austin**, City (pop., 2020: 961,855), capital of Texas, U.S. It was founded in 1835 as the village of Waterloo on the Colorado River in south-central Texas. In 1839 it was made capital of the Republic of Texas and renamed to honour Stephen Austin; when Texas became a state in 1845, Austin was its capital.\", \"page_age\": \"1790 days ago\"}, {\"type\": \"web_search_result\", \"title\": \"Austin, Texas\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/geography-and-cartography/austin-texas/\", \"content\": \"Austin, Texas, is the capital city of the state and a significant cultural and political hub. Founded in 1839, it has grown into one of the largest and most prosperous cities in the U.S., with a population of approximately 974,447 as of 2022, \n","stderr":"","return_code":0,"content":[],"abort_reason":null}}          }

